<title>SWEDEN: Volvo owners approve share capital reduction.</title>
<headline>Volvo owners approve share capital reduction.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish vehicle maker AB Volvo said on Thursday shareholders approved the reduction of share capital by 113 million crowns as a result of its share redemption programme.</p>
<p>Volvo said in a statement that shareholders also approved the board's proposal to increase share capital through a bonus issue and write-up of the share's par value to six crowns from five crowns.</p>
<p>AB Volvo shares will total 441.5 million, or 138.6 million A series shares and 302.9 B series shares, it said.</p>
<p>-- Abigail Schmelz, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700-1003</p>
